timestamp=2026-11-14T21:11:14.896Z level=INFO run=7c5722be message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 -c '\n# Effective cost per kH-month comparison\n# 1. Gen H bought from vendor at month 0 ($25M), delivered month 3 (usable months 3..23 = 21 months)\n# At month 24, marked at 75% * 25 * 0.96^24 * 0.5 = 3.5195M\n# Power in us: 1.4 * 0.15 = 0.21M/mo. If contracted at m=0, energised at m=5 (24m -> m=5..28 -> 5 extra months = 5*0.21 = 1.05M)\n# Capital cost: ~0.75%/mo on tied-up cash (or 2%/mo if in debt).\n# Wait: $25M at 0.75%/mo over 24m: interest lost ~ 25 * (1.0075^24 - 1) ~ 25 * 0.196 = $4.9M (minus resale value effect)\n# More precisely, NPV / terminal wealth impact at month 24 of spending $C at m_pay and getting $R at m_24:\n# Each $1 spent at month m reduces final cash at m=24 by (1+r)^(24-m) where r=0.0075 (if cash>=0) or 0.02 (if cash<0).\ndef future_cost(amount, m, r=0.0075):\n    return amount * ((1 + r)**(24 - m))\n\n# Suppose Gen H bought at m=0, delivered at m=3, powered m=3..23 (say using spare or new power at m=3..26 -> 3 extra months)\n# Wait: if bought at m=0, paid at m=0 ($25M).\nc_H_m0 = future_cost(25, 0) - 3.5195 + sum(future_cost(0.21, m) for m in range(3, 27))\nprint(f\"Gen H at m=0 (21 usable mos, us, 3 extra power mos): total m24 cost = ${c_H_m0:.2f}M, per kH-mo = ${c_H_m0/21:.3f}M\")\n\n# Suppose Gen H bought at m=0 in ap (power $0.168/mo, 4 extra mos):\nc_H_ap = future_cost(25, 0) - 3.5195 + sum(future_cost(0.168, m) for m in range(3, 28))\nprint(f\"Gen H at m=0 (21 usable mos, ap, 4 extra power mos): total m24 cost = ${c_H_ap:.2f}M, per kH-mo = ${c_H_ap/21:.3f}M\")\n\n# What if Gen H bought at m=0 from Broker A ($27.5M, arrives m=2, 22 usable mos)?\nc_H_brkA = future_cost(27.5, 0) - 3.5195 + sum(future_cost(0.21, m) for m in range(2, 26))\nprint(f\"Gen H Broker A at m=0 (if delivered, 22 mos, us): total m24 cost = ${c_H_brkA:.2f}M, per kH-mo = ${c_H_brkA/22:.3f}M\")\n\n# What if Gen N bought at m=12 ($40M = $20M/kH, arrives m=15, 9 usable mos m=15..23)?\n# Marked at m=24: 0.75 * 40 * 0.96^12 = 18.381M ($9.19M/kH)\n# Power: 0.8 MW/kH * 0.12 (ap) = 0.096M/mo. If power signed m=11, energised m=15..38 (15 extra mos!)\nc_N_m12_ap = future_cost(20, 12) - 9.1906 + sum(future_cost(0.096, m) for m in range(15, 39))\nprint(f\"Gen N at m=12 (9 usable mos, ap, 15 extra power mos): total m24 cost = ${c_N_m12_ap:.2f}M, per kH-mo = ${c_N_m12_ap/9:.3f}M\")\n# What if Gen N replaces Gen H on existing power (power signed at m=0..2, expires m=26..28, only 3 extra mos, and we resell Gen H)?\nc_N_m12_reuse = future_cost(20, 12) - 9.1906 + sum(future_cost(0.096, m) for m in range(15, 24))\nprint(f\"Gen N at m=12 (9 usable mos, reusing existing power): total m24 cost = ${c_N_m12_reuse:.2f}M, per kH-mo = ${c_N_m12_reuse/9:.3f}M\")\n\n# Compare with Cloud Reservations at m=0 (index=1.6):\n# 6m in ap: 1.6 * 1.15 * 0.95 = 1.748/mo\n# 12m in ap: 1.6 * 1.00 * 0.95 = 1.520/mo\n# 24m in ap: 1.6 * 0.90 * 0.95 = 1.368/mo (24 mos: m=1..24 -> 1 extra month = 1.368 * 24 / 23 = 1.427/mo per usable month!)\n# Wait: if signed at m=0, 12m is m=1..12. At launch (say m=12), index drops 25% -> new 12m after launch would be ~1.20 * 0.95 = 1.14/mo!\n# So 6m or 12m BEFORE launch lets you re-contract AFTER launch at 25% lower price!\n# Wait: 6m at m=0 (m=1..6) costs 1.748/mo. 12m at m=0 (m=1..12) costs 1.520/mo.\n# 24m at m=0 (m=1..24, 23 usable mos) costs 24 * 1.368 / 23 = 1.427/mo!\n# Compare 12m at m=0 (1.520/mo) + 12m at m=12 (say 1.14/mo, m=13..24 -> 12*1.14/11 = 1.244/mo) -> avg = 1.38/mo!\nprint(\"Cloud ap m=0: 6m=1.748, 12m=1.520, 24m(eff 23m)=1.427\")\nprint(\"Cloud us m=0: 6m=1.840, 12m=1.600, 24m(eff 23m)=1.503\")\nprint(\"Cloud eu m=0: 6m=2.024, 12m=1.760, 24m(eff 23m)=1.653\")\n'" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
