timestamp=2026-11-14T21:12:32.004Z level=INFO run=7c5722be message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 -c '\n# Tight regime Run 1 (m0..7) simulation:\n# Vendor queue #1 (4k to us): ships ~2k/mo -> 2k at m0 (usable m1), 2k at m1 (usable m2? Wait: us only has 1.6 MW = 1.14k spare power until m8!).\n# Wait: if we move excess unpowered H from us to ap at m1 or m2, it arrives at ap at m2 or m3, where ap has 8 MW (5.71k H)!\n# Vendor queue #2 (4k to ap): ships ~2k/mo at m2, m3 -> usable m3, m4 (or m4, m5)!\n# Broker A (1k to us): if delivered (50%*0.9 + 50%*0.35 = 62.5%), usable m2 (fits in 1.14k spare in us!).\n# Let us check capacity if tight for all of m0..7:\nfor g in [0.04, 0.08]:\n    inf = [6.0 * (1+g)**m for m in range(8)]\n    # Conservative cap without broker A and with us_res(1k 12m) + ap_res(1k 12m):\n    # m0: 10 (H) + 2 (us res) + 0.5 (ap spot) = 12.5\n    # m1: 10 + 1.14 (us spare) + 2 (us res) + 1 (ap res) + 1 (us res new) + 0.5 (ap spot) = 15.64\n    # m2..4: same + say 1.7 moved to ap at m2? Wait: if 2k queued arrives m1, only 1.14k powered; 0.86k unpowered -> move 1k to ap at m1 -> arrives ap at m2!\n    # m2: 10 + 1.14 + 0.86(ap) + 2 + 1 + 1 = 16.0\n    # m3..4: +2k from queued #1 or #2 = 18.0\n    # m5..7: -2 (old us res expires) + 2..4 (order #2 arrives) = 18..20\n    cap = [12.5, 15.64, 16.0, 18.0, 18.0, 16.0, 18.0, 18.0]\n    spare = sum(c - i for c, i in zip(cap, inf))\n    print(f\"g={g:.2f}: inf={sum(inf):.1f}, cap={sum(cap):.1f}, spare={spare:.1f}/60\")\n'" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
