timestamp=2026-11-14T21:13:18.785Z level=INFO run=7c5722be message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 -c '\nimport math\n# Prior P(tight m2)=0.90, P(loose m2)=0.10\n# 1. News = loose (0.75 if loose, 0.25 if tight)\n# 2. Index drift = (1.526 - 1.613)/1.613 = -0.0539\n#    loose ~ N(-0.025, 0.05), tight ~ N(0.04, 0.05)\n# 3. Spot/index = 3.74 / 1.526 = 2.451\n#    loose ~ N(1.1, 1.1*0.3=0.33) or lognormal? Wait: even if N(1.1, 0.33), 2.45 is huge!\n#    Wait: what if noise is multiplicative 30% std on log or uniform [0.7, 1.3]?\n#    Let us check normal std=0.3*mean:\ndef norm_pdf(x, mu, sig):\n    return math.exp(-0.5*((x-mu)/sig)**2) / sig\n\np_t = 0.90 * 0.25 * norm_pdf(-0.0539, 0.04, 0.05) * norm_pdf(2.451, 1.8, 1.8*0.3)\np_l = 0.10 * 0.75 * norm_pdf(-0.0539, -0.025, 0.05) * norm_pdf(2.451, 1.1, 1.1*0.3)\nprint(\"Normal spot noise -> P(tight):\", p_t/(p_t+p_l), \"P(loose):\", p_l/(p_t+p_l))\n# Wait: what if spot noise has heavy tail or is uniform/normal with larger sigma?\n# Either way, we can check directly by reserving in ap!\n'" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
